{"scores":{"design":4,"legibility":4,"visual_communication":4,"coherence":4,"requirements":5},"evidence":{"design":"Slides 1-4 share a consistent navy/teal/orange palette, finding-style titles with a rule underneath, and rounded callout panels. Slide 1 pairs a recommendation card with a KPI row, and slide 3 pairs a table with a risk card. Minor defects: on slide 4 the step labels in the Install/Calibrate/Validate/Monitor boxes are top-aligned, leaving the lower half of each box empty. On slide 3 the table rows have large empty padding below the text. On slide 1 the 'Next gate' bar text sits high in its box.","legibility":"Titles and KPI numbers ($250k / $80k / 3.1 yrs) on slides 1 and 4 are large and high-contrast. On slide 2 the chart data labels (950/980, 840/900, etc.), axis, and legend are readable. Weaker points: the subtitle lines under each title are very small. The grey caption text on slides 1, 3 and 4 (e.g. 'Staged pilot: wider rollout proceeds only if…') is low-contrast. On slide 2 the Q1 '950' label sits close to the 1000 gridline. No clipping is visible.","visual_communication":"Slide 2's clustered actual/target bars with value labels are paired with a gap panel (−30/−60/−110/−70, year −270). That panel highlights Q3 in orange and makes the finding immediately clear. The slide 3 table is clean, and the risk card ties the per-site risks to pilot verification. On slide 4 the process is shown as a sequence ending in an orange Go/No-go node with outcomes labeled. However, the connectors are plain lines without arrowheads, so direction is implied only by left-to-right order.","coherence":"The story follows the required order: financial decision (slide 1) → performance (slide 2) → sites and risk (slide 3) → process and decision (slide 4). Layouts are varied but related, and the go/no-go gate is threaded through slides 1, 3 and 4. Some redundancy: slide 4's dark decision panel repeats slide 1's three KPIs and payback formula almost verbatim.","requirements":"Slide 1: $250k investment, $80k annual saving, 3.1 years payback with a correct calculation (250/80 = 3.125); $220k does not appear anywhere. Slide 2: Q1–Q4 actual 950/840/850/730 vs target 980/900/960/800, with a 'Readings per quarter' label and an Actual/Target legend. The derived totals (3,370 vs 3,640 = 92.6%) and gaps are correct. Slide 3: the table has North 330/95%/Staffing, Central 490/86%/Hardware, South 310/88%/Training; 490 of 1,130 = 43% is correct. The slide 3 risk card reads 'Verify the pilot before wider rollout'. Slide 4: Install > Calibrate > Validate > Monitor are connected and followed by a Go/No-go checkpoint after the pilot. Exactly four slides, all titles state findings, and no slide is only a cover."},"checks":[true,true,true,true,true,true,true,true,true,true,true,true],"worst_slide":4,"most_important_fix":"On slide 4, replace the plain connector lines with arrowheads to make the Install→Calibrate→Validate→Monitor→Go/No-go flow explicitly directional, and vertically center the step labels in their boxes. Also replace the duplicated KPI block with pilot-specific go/no-go criteria (e.g. readings or on-time thresholds) so the slide adds decision content instead of repeating slide 1."}
```

